      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b1b6559605741536af2f13b|full_name}: Yes, I definitely understand that. What I'm suggesting, though, is definitely NOT to make it look dirty. The roughness and smudge overlay would be so subtle that you wouldn't even notice it consciously unless you were looking SPECIFICALLY for it. But the spatial recognition part of our brain DOES notice the tiny distortions in the mirror's surface as our eyes pass over them, and whenever we move. It's why we generally don't walk into mirrors or windows in real life, but it happens all the time in VRChat mirrors, if they're not obviously up against a wall, and not floor-to-ceiling. You'd still see what others do, the same way you would when looking in a clean mirror in real life.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
