  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-08-04T06:51:13.672Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, VRC mirrors are a PERFECT mirror. If you don't KNOW they're there, they look like an open air. In real life, mirrors are not 100% reflective. They have a minute amount of roughness to them, which makes them look solid. Not to mention, even the cleanest mirrors have a tiny amount of residual smudges just from interacting with the world. The roughness is something that can be fixed by changing a line or two in the mirror shader. A smudge texture overlay would take a little more effort, but really not that much. Neither of these would impact performance AT ALL because they take place after the mirror has rendered the reflection, and are one of the simplest forms of texture multiplication.",
